{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"To access the print version of the article, a link is provided. The rules for the Sudoku puzzle are explained, with a key exception being that the numbers in cells within grey lines must sum up to the figures in the corner. This unique twist adds a new layer of complexity to the traditional puzzle. The standard rules of Sudoku still apply, with the constraint that no number can be repeated within each shape formed by the grey lines. This ensures that the puzzle remains challenging and requires careful consideration.\"\n\n\n \nAddition to the traditional Sudoku rules, the numbers in the cells contained within grey lines have a specific requirement. They must add up to the figures in the corner, which is a crucial detail to keep in mind while solving the puzzle. The constraint of not repeating numbers within each shape formed by grey lines is also essential to remember. By following these rules, solvers can ensure that they are on the right track to completing the puzzle. The unique combination of traditional and modified rules makes this Sudoku puzzle an exciting challenge.\n\n\n \nThe Sudoku puzzle is presented in a way that is both familiar and innovative. The use of grey lines to form shapes and the requirement for numbers to add up to the figures in the corner are distinctive features. Solvers who are accustomed to traditional Sudoku puzzles will need to adapt to these new elements in order to succeed. The puzzle is designed to be engaging and demanding, with a unique set of rules that must be carefully followed. By embracing this challenge, solvers can develop their problem-solving skills and enjoy the satisfaction of completing the puzzle.\n\n\n \nThe opportunity to view the completed puzzle is available to those who purchase next week's Observer Digital Edition. This provides a chance for solvers to check their work and see the solution to the puzzle. The completed puzzle can serve as a useful reference, helping solvers to understand how the rules were applied and how the solution was achieved. By examining the completed puzzle, solvers can gain a deeper understanding of the Sudoku rules and improve their skills for future puzzles.\n\n\n \nThe Sudoku puzzle is a challenging and entertaining activity that requires careful attention to the rules and constraints. By following the traditional Sudoku rules, as well as the additional requirements for the numbers in the cells within grey lines, solvers can enjoy the process of solving the puzzle. The sense of accomplishment that comes from completing the puzzle is rewarding, and the opportunity to view the completed puzzle in the Observer Digital Edition is an added bonus. The puzzle is a fun and engaging way to exercise the mind and develop problem-solving skills.", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"To", "logprob": -0.4018803536891937}, {"token": " access", "logprob": -0.04305700585246086}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0232519693672657}, {"token": " print", "logprob": -0.008725020103156567}, {"token": " version", "logprob": -7.486063259420916e-05}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0031777145341038704}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.011118361726403236}, {"token": " article", "logprob": -0.2270030528306961}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.002512990264222026}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.024781323969364166}, {"token": " link", "logprob": -0.008299149572849274}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0067192567512393}, {"token": " provided", "logprob": -0.00012361239350866526}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.31154054403305054}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.0039595551788806915}, {"token": " rules", "logprob": -0.11019902676343918}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.02659463882446289}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.8281631469726562}, {"token": " Sudoku", "logprob": -0.047784850001335144}, {"toke